# tally 2.1.8 R5 (#162's rest, pick P29; T's m2/g1/n1_law): an ask's law expression is read with no law date, so
# one that reaches an at reader def (n_after) is refused at load, whatever the asks, in the words run gave it.
# 2.1.8's first refcore found it at run, so an ask that doesn't reach it (q_plain) answered.
=== m.tally
model pr
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "made up"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

axis pa
  lo "lower pay"
  hi "higher pay"

place kasa: claims DUK lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input p_lo: money DUK

input p_hi: money DUK

input d1: date

input d2: date

input fee: money DUK

def n_after: money DUK = sum(x.cash.amount for x in transfers over d1..d2) at reader

def pay: money DUK at d1
  rule base = p_lo
  rule hi beats base = p_hi when pa == hi

move salary: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to kasa amount pay

move charge: transfers
  on d2
  leg cash from kasa to world amount fee






version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  p_lo = 5.00
  p_hi = 20.00
  d1 = 2026-03-01
  d2 = 2026-03-02
  fee = 10.00

ask q_law: fee law (if n_after > fee then 2026-10-25 else 2026-10-24)

ask q_plain: n_after law 2026-10-25
=== expect q_plain
refused: LOAD-LAWDATE ask reaches an at reader def (n_after) without law
